Marta: Heads-up — we're seeing a perf regression in canary for short sequences (<=32). After the kernel-selector tweak yesterday, p50 looks fine but p95/p99 for small requests is ~2.3x slower. Root cause trace looks like the smem-optimized kernel is being chosen even when seq_len is tiny and batches are small.

Yi-Kim: Repro confirmed locally. small-seq cases get into the smem path because the selector logic was only checking feature flags + device_family, not seq_len distribution. For seq_len<=32 we should prefer low-smem, lower-reg-pressure kernel. :eyes:

Ravi: Profiling flame output (short summary): smem kernel -> high shared mem usage -> register spilling -> increased L1 thrash -> lower occupancy. Compare: occupancy ~38% for smem path vs ~72% for the low-smem kernel on same batch.

Phil: Quick idea: add a gating rule in kernel-picker based on seq_len histogram and batch_tokens estimate. Something like: if median_seq <= 48 AND estimated_tokens_per_sm >= threshold then prefer small-kernel.

Yi-Kim: Prototype decision rule I ran:
```
// pseudo
if (device == A100 && median_seq <= 48) {
  pick = kernel_small_reg_friendly;
} else if (smem_required && median_seq > 64) {
  pick = kernel_smem_high_throughput;
} else {
  pick = kernel_default_heuristic();
}
```
This removed the regression on my local canary.

Marta: Nice. We also see KV cache prefetching touching shared memory for the smem kernel (the prefetch buffer landed in SMem). That exacerbates reg pressure. Could we try moving prefetch buffer out of SMem for small-seq path?

Ravi: Yes — two low-risk experiments: (A) gating kernel picker by seq_len histogram (fast), (B) change KV prefetch memclass to global for small-kernel only (safer but needs testing for bandwidth). I ran (A) and perf looks good. (B) needs validation on large batches because global-prefetch increases latency in large-seq cases.

Phil: I ran autotune sweep across tile_size x warp_specialization for seq_len buckets [8,16,32,64,128]. Results: smaller tile_size + disable warp_specialization wins for seq<=32. For seq>=128, the smem-specialized path still wins. So selector must be seq_len-aware AND prefer disabling warp-specialization for short sequences.

ops-bot: Canary deploy: kernel-picker patch v0.1 rolled to canary cluster (canary-3). Monitor channels: #eng-runtime-perf.

Marta: Action items: 1) Yi-Kim to land seq_len gating in picker (feature-flagged). 2) Ravi to run KV prefetch global-mem experiment in canary A/B (10% traffic). 3) Phil to add autotune results to the model profile DB (so picker can consult). 4) roll back plan if p99 increases. I'll draft the rollout plan after we have A/B numbers.

Yi-Kim: On it — I'll push the gated rule + unit tests. Will include a tiny sim that samples seq hist and asserts the pick. PR later today. :thumbsup:

Ravi: I'll schedule the KV-prefetch A/B for tomorrow morning and attach perf dashboards.

Phil: I'll upload the sweep csv and add mapping in model-profile service so the picker can query bucketed results.

